From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:52:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3399: add the Rigol DHO800/DHO900 and MHO900
 board

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

NovaOS local patch. The RK3399 main board of Rigol's DHO800/DHO900 and
MHO900 oscilloscopes, one defconfig per family:

- LPDDR4, 2 channels x 32 bit, 1 rank, 4 GiB: PMUGRF OS_REG2 reads
  0x32C1F2C1 on these boards, so the TPL uses
  rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-100.dtsi, the only LPDDR4 timing set in the tree,
  with CONFIG_RAM_ROCKCHIP_LPDDR4; sdram_rk3399.c detects the rank,
  column, bank and row counts itself.
- The SD card on SDMMC0 is the only boot medium; u-boot.itb sits in the
  card's zero gap at LBA 2048 (SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x800,
  SPL_PAD_TO=0xf8000), never at the default 0x4000, which is the start
  of the scope's uboot partition.
- Console UART2 at 115200; SPL_ATF_NO_PLATFORM_PARAM is off, so BL31
  takes the same rate from /chosen/stdout-path.
- Rockusb (2207:330c) on OTG0 for Loader mode; no watchdog, no ADC
  download key, no Android BCB code (misc offset 0 holds a stale
  --wipe_all), no saved environment, no network.
- ROCKCHIP_MASKROM_IMAGE for a RAM boot over USB.

The board code (board/rigol/rigol_rk3399/rigol_rk3399.c) keeps what the
systems on the card expect of their boot loader:
- the reboot flag in PMUGRF OS_REG0 is read in
  rockchip_early_misc_init_r(), before setup_boot_mode() clears it: low
  byte 1 and 0x1888aaff are Loader, 3 is recovery, everything else (6 and
  7, the stock "wipe data", included) a normal boot (rigol_bootflag.h);
- SPL opens UART0 at 1,500,000 baud (GPIO2_C0/C1 only) before it loads
  U-Boot; on a normal boot U-Boot scans every frame received since then
  plus RIGOL_RUNSTOP_WINDOW_MS for Run/Stop (FA 08 0C 34 AF or
  FA 08 00 58 AF), which enters Loader mode;
- otherwise it sends the power-on-mode frame FA 05 05 0A AF (auto).

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
